Mr. Stewart: The range of services made available by national health service provider units to general practitioners does not vary according to whether or not they are fund holders. Rather than relying on the health board's purchasing arrangements, GP fund holders are able to use their funds to purchase the following hospital and community health services directly from providers:


—a specified range of elective surgical procedures;

—most out-patient treatments and diagnostic tests;

—certain specified direct access services;

and from 1 April 1993:


—certain community nursing services;

—additional direct access services;

—most out patient mental health treatments.

